<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William McKinley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a>–<a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William McKinley was the 25th President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, from 1897 until his assassination in 1901. A Republican from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>, he led the country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a> of 1898, which brought the annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, Guam and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, and he also annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>. His proclamation of 'benevolent assimilation' set American policy in the Philippines, where his forces fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-mckinley.jpg" alt="William McKinley" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:McKinley_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
